IMPORT prelude

-- Pharmacists Registration Act 2007 (Singapore) -- who may practise pharmacy and what happens to those who do without
-- authority: the "unauthorised person" (s 2) and the training exemption (s 70); the Schedule's list of acts constituting the
-- practice of pharmacy; the s 28 offences and their defence, employer and pharmacist liability (ss 29, 30), suspended persons
-- (s 31) and the general penalty (s 35); eligibility for full, conditional and temporary registration (ss 16, 17, 19); the
-- registered pharmacist's own duties and deadlines (ss 15(4)-(6), 23, 24(c)(iii)); the Disciplinary Committee's sanctions,
-- when its orders take effect and the appeal (ss 45(2), 46(7)-(11), 47); restoration of a removed name (ss 26(2), 48(2)); and
-- composition of offences (s 69).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021, in operation from 31 December 2021), informal
-- consolidation, version in force from 5/12/2025, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PRA2007.txt. The latest
-- amendment annotated in the text is Act 19 of 2025 w.e.f. 05/12/2025 (s 69, composition). The body's section numbers are
-- followed; the arrangement at the top of the deposit runs one behind from s 21 (it omits "Application for registration" as
-- a numbered entry).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0019 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. SCOPED to what a pharmacist, a would-be pharmacist, a pharmacy-owning employer or a member of the
-- public meets. Not encoded: the Council, the Specialists Accreditation Board and their constitution (Parts 2, 5); the
-- registers' contents beyond the change-of-particulars duty; specialist registration (s 18) beyond the title offence; the
-- complaints procedure, the Health Committee and interim orders (ss 38-44, 50-60); inspectors (s 65); fees (none are fixed in
-- the Act); and the Council's discretions to refuse registration (s 21(5)) and remove names (s 25(1)), which are not
-- rule-shaped.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Pharmacists Registration Act 2007 -- practice`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `Schedule -- the practice of pharmacy`

-- s 2: "practice of pharmacy" means any of the acts or activities specified in the Schedule. Schedule para 1: applying the
-- knowledge and science of pharmacy in (a) interpreting, evaluating and implementing prescriptions; (b) "compounding,
-- labelling, dispensing, distributing and administering medication"; (c) initiating and modifying medication therapy under
-- collaborative practice agreements; (d) "patient assessment and counselling for the purpose of recommending and dispensing
-- medication"; (e) managing medication therapy; (f) evaluating medication use; (g) manufacturing and distributing medicinal
-- products, oral dental gums and therapeutic products; (h) quality assurance of them.
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `filling a doctor's prescription`
    `dispensing medication`
    `counselling a patient to recommend a medicine`
    `modifying therapy under a collaborative practice agreement`
    `manufacturing therapeutic products`
    `quality assurance of medicinal products`
    `keeping the pharmacy's accounts`
    `stacking shelves`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is the practice of pharmacy` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `keeping the pharmacy's accounts` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `stacking shelves` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `2 and 70 -- the unauthorised person`

-- s 2: "unauthorised person" means "(a) a person who is not a registered pharmacist; or (b) a registered pharmacist who does
-- not have a valid practising certificate, and who has not been exempted under section 70 or 71."
-- s 70: nothing in this Act prevents an act within the practice of pharmacy if carried out "(a) in the course of the person's
-- training; (b) under the supervision of a pharmacist registered under section 16(1); and (c) in an establishment approved by
-- the Council". s 71: the Minister may exempt any person or class by order in the Gazette.
DECLARE Person HAS
    `registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a valid practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in training` IS A BOOLEAN
    `supervised by a pharmacist registered under section 16(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at a Council-approved establishment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempted by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person has the training exemption` IF
        `the person`'s `in training`
    AND `the person`'s `supervised by a pharmacist registered under section 16(1)`
    AND `the person`'s `at a Council-approved establishment`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is unauthorised` IF
        ((NOT `the person`'s `registered`) OR (NOT `the person`'s `holds a valid practising certificate`))
    AND (NOT `the person has the training exemption` `the person`)
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `exempted by the Minister`)

§§ `28 -- unauthorised person acting as pharmacist`

-- s 28(1): an unauthorised person is guilty of an offence if the person (a) practises pharmacy; (b) "wilfully and falsely
-- pretends to be a duly qualified pharmacist"; (c) practises under the style or title of a pharmacist; (d) "takes or uses the
-- name or title of pharmacist, pharmaceutical chemist, druggist, apothecary"; (e) uses any name, title, sign, uniform or badge
-- implying qualification; or (f) "advertises or holds himself or herself out as a pharmacist".
-- s 28(2): "It is a defence to a prosecution under subsection (1)(a) if the defendant proves that he or she did not in any way
-- represent himself or herself as a duly qualified or registered pharmacist." The defence is to limb (a) only.
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `practising pharmacy`
    `pretending to be a qualified pharmacist`
    `calling oneself a druggist or apothecary`
    `wearing a pharmacist's badge or uniform`
    `advertising as a pharmacist`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `proved no representation as a pharmacist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits an offence under section 28` IF
        `the person is unauthorised` `the person`
    AND CONSIDER `the conduct`
        WHEN `practising pharmacy` THEN NOT `proved no representation as a pharmacist`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `29 and 30 -- employers and pharmacists who let it happen`

-- s 29(1): where a s 28 offence is committed by an unauthorised person "acting as an employee, an agent or a partner of another
-- person, that other person shall also be guilty of an offence". (2): defence if the defendant proves the offence was committed
-- "without the defendant's knowledge" AND that the defendant "has taken all reasonable precautions and exercised due diligence".
GIVEN `the worker offended under section 28` IS A BOOLEAN, `the worker is an employee, agent or partner` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved lack of knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved reasonable precautions and due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer commits an offence under section 29` IF
        `the worker offended under section 28`
    AND `the worker is an employee, agent or partner`
    AND NOT (`proved lack of knowledge` AND `proved reasonable precautions and due diligence`)

-- s 30(1): a registered pharmacist who "allows an unauthorised person to practise pharmacy ... on any premises used by or under
-- the control of that registered pharmacist"; (2) who "has knowingly enabled" an unauthorised person "whether described as an
-- assistant or otherwise"; (4) who practises on premises where an unauthorised person practises, "knowing or having reason to
-- believe" it. (3): defence to (1) and (2) only -- mistake, reliance on information, another's act or cause beyond control,
-- AND reasonable precautions and due diligence.
DECLARE Involvement IS ONE OF
    `allowed it on premises the pharmacist controls`
    `knowingly enabled it as an assistant`
    `practised alongside knowing of it`

GIVEN `the involvement` IS AN Involvement, `proved mistake or cause beyond control` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved precautions and diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pharmacist commits an offence under section 30` IF
    CONSIDER `the involvement`
    WHEN `practised alongside knowing of it` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOT (`proved mistake or cause beyond control` AND `proved precautions and diligence`)

-- s 31: a person whose registration "has been suspended under Part 6 must not practise pharmacy during the period of his or
-- her suspension". s 46(12): while suspended the person "is not to be regarded as being registered", and rights revive on
-- expiry only if "the pharmacist has complied with all the terms of the order".
GIVEN `suspended under Part 6` IS A BOOLEAN, `within the suspension period` IS A BOOLEAN, `practised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits an offence under section 31` IF
    `suspended under Part 6` AND `within the suspension period` AND `practised`

§§ `35 -- general penalty`

-- s 35: an offence under s 28(1), 29(1), 30(1), (2) or (4), 31(2), 32(2) or 33(2) -- "a fine not exceeding $25,000 and, in the
-- case of a second or subsequent conviction for an offence under any of those sections, to a fine not exceeding $50,000 or to
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both". A first conviction carries no imprisonment.
GIVEN `previously convicted under a section 35 offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 35` MEANS
    IF `previously convicted under a section 35 offence` THEN 50000 ELSE 25000

GIVEN `previously convicted under a section 35 offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment under section 35` MEANS
    IF `previously convicted under a section 35 offence` THEN 6 ELSE 0

-- s 69(1): the Council may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum not exceeding the
-- lower of (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $2,000". [Act 19 of 2025
-- wef 05/12/2025.] Which offences are prescribed is left to regulations (s 69(3)), not retrieved.
GIVEN `the prescribed maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`the prescribed maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 2000

§§ `16, 17, 19 -- eligibility for registration`

-- s 16(1): eligible for full registration if the person "(a) holds a Singapore degree; and (b) has acquired at least 12 months'
-- practical experience ... at any establishment approved by the Council, of which at least 9 months have been acquired under
-- the supervision of a fully registered pharmacist at an establishment in Singapore". (s 16(2), (3): Council discretions, not
-- encoded.)
GIVEN `holds a Singapore degree` IS A BOOLEAN, `months of approved practical experience` IS A NUMBER,
      `months supervised in Singapore` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is eligible for full registration` IF
        `holds a Singapore degree`
    AND `months of approved practical experience` AT LEAST 12
    AND `months supervised in Singapore` AT LEAST 9

-- s 17(1): a prescribed (or equivalent) foreign qualification makes a person eligible for conditional registration, but by
-- s 17(3) not entitled unless the person "(a) has acquired at least 12 months' practical experience ... of which at least
-- 3 months have been acquired under the supervision of a fully registered pharmacist at an establishment in Singapore; (b) has
-- been selected for employment in Singapore as a pharmacist" in an approved institution; and "(c) has sat for and passed such
-- examination as the Council may prescribe".
GIVEN `holds a prescribed foreign qualification` IS A BOOLEAN, `months of approved practical experience` IS A NUMBER,
      `months supervised in Singapore` IS A NUMBER, `selected for employment in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `passed the Council's examination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is entitled to conditional registration` IF
        `holds a prescribed foreign qualification`
    AND `months of approved practical experience` AT LEAST 12
    AND `months supervised in Singapore` AT LEAST 3
    AND `selected for employment in Singapore`
    AND `passed the Council's examination`

-- s 19(3): temporary registration "is for a period not exceeding 2 years which may be renewed ... for a further period or
-- periods each not exceeding 12 months".
GIVEN `is a renewal` IS A BOOLEAN, `months granted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the temporary registration period is within section 19(3)` IF
    IF `is a renewal` THEN `months granted` AT MOST 12 ELSE `months granted` AT MOST 24

§§ `15(4)-(6), 23, 24(c)(iii) -- the registered pharmacist's own deadlines`

-- s 15(4)(a): a registered pharmacist must inform the Registrar in writing of a change in name, residential address or practice
-- address "within 28 days of the change"; (5) $1,000 fine; (6) a report of a change of residential address under s 10 of the
-- National Registration Act 1965 is deemed compliance on the date it is made.
GIVEN `days after the change when told` IS A NUMBER, `change was of residential address reported under the NRA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the change of particulars was notified in time` IF
        `days after the change when told` AT MOST 28
    OR  `change was of residential address reported under the NRA`

-- s 23(2): a practising certificate is granted "for a period not exceeding 2 years". (3)(a): a renewal application must be
-- "made no later than one month before the expiry"; (4) a pharmacist who applies later "is liable to pay ... such late
-- application fee as the Council may prescribe" (the amount is not in the Act).
GIVEN `months before expiry the renewal was made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a late application fee is payable` IF
    `months before expiry the renewal was made` LESS THAN 1

-- s 23(6): a person whose registration is cancelled or suspended under Part 6 must surrender the practising certificate
-- "(a) within 14 days of being notified" or (b) where an appeal is pending, within the period the Council specifies; (7) $1,000.
GIVEN `days since notified` IS A NUMBER, `surrendered` IS A BOOLEAN, `appeal pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is in breach of section 23(6)` IF
        (NOT `surrendered`)
    AND (NOT `appeal pending`)
    AND `days since notified` GREATER THAN 14

-- s 24(c)(iii): the Registrar must remove the name of a person "who has not renewed his or her practising certificate for a
-- continuous period of at least 5 years".
GIVEN `continuous years without renewing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must remove the name` IF
    `continuous years without renewing` AT LEAST 5

§§ `45, 46, 47 -- the Disciplinary Committee`

-- s 45(2): the Committee may (a) remove the name; (b) "suspend the registration ... for a period of at least 3 months but not
-- more than 3 years"; (c) impose conditions "for a period not exceeding 3 years"; (d) "impose ... a penalty not exceeding
-- $50,000"; (e) censure; (f) a letter of advice or warning; (g) an undertaking; (h) any other order.
DECLARE Sanction HAS
    `months of suspension` IS A NUMBER
    `months of conditions` IS A NUMBER
    `penalty` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the sanction` IS A Sanction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sanction is within section 45(2)` IF
        (`the sanction`'s `months of suspension` EQUALS 0 OR (`the sanction`'s `months of suspension` AT LEAST 3 AND `the sanction`'s `months of suspension` AT MOST 36))
    AND `the sanction`'s `months of conditions` AT MOST 36
    AND `the sanction`'s `penalty` AT MOST 50000

-- s 46(7): an order for removal or suspension under s 45(2) "does not take effect until the expiry of 30 days after the order
-- is made"; (8) unless the Committee orders it to take effect immediately for the protection of the public or in the
-- pharmacist's interest -- then (9) from the time made if the pharmacist was present or represented, (10) otherwise from
-- service of notice. (11) every other order "takes effect from the time the order is made".
-- s 47(1): appeal to the General Division of the High Court "within 30 days after the service ... of the notice of the order";
-- (2) no further appeal. (4): "Despite section 45 or 46", where a person has appealed against an order under s 45(2) or 46,
-- "the order does not take effect unless" confirmed, or the appeal is dismissed or withdrawn.
-- Day counting is an inference: day 30 is within "30 days"; the 30-day wait ends at the close of day 30.
-- LITERAL READING: s 47(4) is not limited to orders under s 46(7), so on its words an appeal holds off even an immediate
-- order under s 46(8). The encoding follows the words; the point is flagged in NOTES.md.
DECLARE Order IS ONE OF
    `removal from the register`
    `suspension`
    `financial penalty`
    `censure`

GIVEN `the order` IS AN Order, `days since the order was made` IS A NUMBER, `immediate order under section 46(8)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `present, represented or served` IS A BOOLEAN, `appeal undetermined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order is in effect` IF
        (NOT `appeal undetermined`)
    AND CONSIDER `the order`
        WHEN `removal from the register` THEN `days since the order was made` GREATER THAN 30 OR (`immediate order under section 46(8)` AND `present, represented or served`)
        WHEN `suspension` THEN `days since the order was made` GREATER THAN 30 OR (`immediate order under section 46(8)` AND `present, represented or served`)
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `days after service of notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal to the High Court is in time` IF
    `days after service of notice` AT MOST 30

§§ `26(2), 48(2) -- getting a name back`

-- s 48(2): an application to restore a name removed by a Disciplinary Committee must not be made "(a) before the expiry of
-- 3 years from the date of the removal of the name; or (b) more than once in any period of 12 months ... and unless the
-- pharmacist has complied with all the terms of the order".
GIVEN `months since removal` IS A NUMBER, `months since last application` IS A NUMBER, `complied with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a restoration application may be made after disciplinary removal` IF
        `months since removal` AT LEAST 36
    AND `months since last application` AT LEAST 12
    AND `complied with the order`

-- s 26(1)-(2): a name removed for not renewing for 5 years (s 24(c)(iii)) or for breach of registration conditions
-- (s 25(1)(a), (b)) may be restored on application, but an application "must not be made ... more than once in any period of
-- 6 months". There is no waiting period from removal. (s 26(3) compliance with any s 25 order is not modelled.)
GIVEN `months since last application` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a restoration application may be made after administrative removal` IF
    `months since last application` AT LEAST 6
